{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be","id":1468828,"title":"How many disciplines should there be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-25T04:49:04-08:00","id":1468828,"title":"How many disciplines should there be?","content":"Different books give us different ideas. From the 10 in V5 to the wild lists of prior editions with potentially an infinite amount of unique inceptor disciplines. How do you group/merge disciplines, or have you written a long list of strange powers for your thinbloods. <br /> <br /> My list<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Animalism<br /> Auspex (Some of Mytherceria is a variant one can learn by hunting changelings)<br /> Celerity<br /> Dominate<br /> Fortitude<br /> Obfuscate<br /> Potence<br /> Presence<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy (Including most other types of sorcery. many inceptor disciplines are unknowingly thaumaturgy. Bardo is here) <br /> Protean (Serpentis, Thanatosis and Visceraticka are Variants, as are most inceptor disciplines. Protean doesn't have paths, vampires can learn abilities out of order so long as it's of appropriate level.)<br /> <br /> Chimestry<br /> Countermagic<br /> Dark Thaumaturgy (which is added upon standard thaumaturgy, up to the limit of generational maximums. So someone with 2 dots of Thaum and 1 dot of DT is a level 3 thaumaturge) <br /> Flight<br /> That singing one. <br /> Mortis (Just a better name for necromancy) <br /> Obtenebration<br /> Quietus<br /> Valeren (diamonion, Obeah) <br /> Vicissitude (Sanguinis is a path, also sanguinis can be used with anyone you share a bond with that also knows the discipline. Join us, Join us, Join us.) <br /> &quot;Spirit mastery&quot; (koldunic sorcery: ogham is rituals)<br /> <br /> Things I'm on the fence about<b></b>: Dementation. As much as it's linked to Dominate, it's far too diffferent. As much as I like <i>passion </i>I think Dominate malks are better. It would make a great thaumaturgy path... but I don't think malks should be challenging the Tremere and learning magic is just a different vibe to ordinary disciplines, it's quite unfitting) <br /> Things that mostly probably shouldn't exist: Abombwe (fold into abyss mysticism?), Spiritus (Fold into Valeren/Diamonion or Thaumaturgy?) Temporis (Thaumaturgy throw in?) </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T05:34:26-08:00","id":1468834,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that the different approaches to Blood Magic could be folded onto a single Discipline, perhaps having a sub-trait (like Paths and Rituals are) to determine what kind fo magic you're cappable of.<br /> <br /> I like the concept of learned magicians having studied magics from all over the world, but learning many Disciplines it's too cumbersome - to the point even ppl that are powerful enough to bypass the social/political barriers to do so, won't. This &quot;policy&quot; ends with some degree of overlap when players (and sometimes, authors) start making Paths/Rituals that resemble those of other Disciplines, whenever they think their wizard would look cool with those powers. I think it can get awkward<br /> <br /> Instead of making a &quot;Path of Summoning Storms&quot;, and then another Path for the &quot;Spirit mastery&quot; Discipline so the shamans can do that too, just make one Path - the rest it's &quot;how you do it&quot; (taking a page from mage, it's Pardigm/Focus). Saves a lot of embarrasement for when you feel your wizards should be able to do stuff that's better covered by another Discipline, and could even reduce the number of Paths a little","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T10:08:23-08:00","id":1468845,"title":"","content":"I'm fond of V5's 10 well defined disciplines, especially the changes to Chimermistry, Serpentis and Quietus. Personally, the few disciplines that don't work as amalgams aren't really worth being brought back, like Temporis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T10:37:20-08:00","id":1468848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468845#post1468845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fond of V5's 10 well defined disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not allowed to make this a V5 bashing thread but V5's disciplines are not <i>well defined</i> they're loose collections of powers held together by theme. V1 Fortitude negates more and more damage, That's well defined. V5 fortitude is anything from &quot;you have more health&quot; to &quot;you ignore one attack per turn&quot; to &quot;insults upset you less&quot; which is... less cohesive. I'll grant that V5 does a relatively decent job with Presence, but Presence has always been the messy kid in vampire. <br /> <br /> ...and I really hate picking powers, at least how V5 does it.. V5 offers more choices, but as you can only have 5 powers in a discipline, every choice locks you off from another choice. That's very stressful. A linear 1-5 system with some powers having options to buy alternative powers you didn't get is elegant in it's simplicity; There's no overchoice, there's no locking yourself out of a power. When I buy a power in V20, I'm only sacrificing XP and delaying the acquisition of other options. When I buy a power in V5, I need to think deeply about the &quot;build&quot; that I want because there's a hard cap on what I can get. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T11:11:22-08:00","id":1468856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468848#post1468848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not allowed to make this a V5 bashing thread but V5's disciplines are not <i>well defined</i> they're loose collections of powers held together by theme. V1 Fortitude negates more and more damage, That's well defined. V5 fortitude is anything from &quot;you have more health&quot; to &quot;you ignore one attack per turn&quot; to &quot;insults upset you less&quot; which is... less cohesive. I'll grant that V5 does a relatively decent job with Presence, but Presence has always been the messy kid in vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a disciple focused on resisting. It mostly adds old elder level powers as normal 1-5 powers, some of which focused on mind-stuff, so that even if your character always avoid combat, they get some use out of it. Or if they just don't focus to hard on it and keep it at one dot. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T11:31:26-08:00","id":1468858,"title":"","content":"Mostly use the ones from Revised, though I fiddle with them from time to time. Replacing Serpentis's level one power with Daimonion's Sense the Sin, for example, or just giving Gargoyles their own variation of Protean which alters the third through fifth level powers to allow them to merge with stone/concrete, grow wings, and turn to stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T12:07:00-08:00","id":1468860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468848#post1468848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not allowed to make this a V5 bashing thread</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try and avoid edition warring here too, but generally, I've got to say V5's 12 disciplines has proven more than sufficient for everything I've needed to run. I don't really see a need to further breakdown or separate powers under different discipline headings as V20 did.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5's disciplines are not <i>well defined</i> they're loose collections of powers held together by theme. </div> </div> </div>I have to respectfully disagree, the theme and power types are cohesive and consistent. V5 disciplines combine the powers that can share fundamental mechanics, which can then be altered by flavour as needed. (E.g. Thaumaturgical Blood Sorcery vs Quietus Blood Sorcery doesn't really need fundamentally different mechanics, just differences in terms of description.)<br /> <br /> <b>1) Animalism - </b>Control animals and the nature of animals.<br /> <b>2) Auspex - </b>Augmenting senses including attuning them to 'magic', or giving you extra-sensory perception.<br /> <b>3) Blood Sorcery -</b> Vampiric magic (typically in the form of exerting 'control' over the blood), combining the schools of practice.<br /> <b>4) Celerity - </b>Speed and grace.<br /> <b>5) Dominate -</b> Direct mental control over others, including memories.<br /> <b>6) Fortitude -</b> Greater resistance to damage physical or mental.<br /> <b>7) Obfuscate -</b> Misdirecting senses to go unnoticed.<br /> <b>8) Oblivion - </b>Control/utilisation of the Abyss/Shadowlands and their manifestations in the skinlands.<br /> <b>9) Potence -</b> Greater strength channelled to various effects.<br /> <b>10) Presence -</b> Control over the emotions of others.<br /> <b>11) Protean - </b>Shape-changing and manipulating organic matter.<br /> <b>12) Thin-Blood Alchemy -</b> Altering the properties of Thin-Blood vitae with certain ingredients. <i>(The only one that I'm shakey on really, still feels like they just wanted to give something cool to the Thin-Bloods. It could just as easily have been another type of Blood Sorcery, predominantly used by Thin-Bloods and requiring their vitae.)</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T12:45:31-08:00","id":1468864,"title":"","content":"Well, since you asked...<br /> <br /> My answer is thirty. Thirty disciplines. But only a third of them see anything approaching common usage in a given chronicle (the original ten disciplines). Roughly another third of them are for groups that operate mostly outside of normal Kindred society (the independents and the Sabbat). The last third of them are so rare that they are, in practical terms, NPC powers only (bloodline and inceptor disciplines, and so on).<br /> <br /> In other words, pretty much 2nd Edition by the book. There are no surprises here:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>The Original Ten</b><br /> Animalism<br /> Auspex<br /> Celerity<br /> Dominate<br /> Fortitude<br /> Obfuscate<br /> Potence<br /> Presence<br /> Protean<br /> Thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> <b>Independent Only</b><br /> Chimerstry<br /> Necromancy<br /> Quietus<br /> Serpentis<br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat Only</b><br /> Dementation<br /> Obtenebration<br /> Vicissitude<br /> <br /> <b>Odds and Ends</b><br /> Bardo<br /> Daimonion<br /> Dark Thaumaturgy<br /> Kineticism<br /> Melpominee<br /> Mytherceria<br /> Nihilistics<br /> Obeah<br /> Sanguinus<br /> Spiritus<br /> Temporis<br /> Thanatosis<br /> Visceratika</div></div> </div> </div><br /> I've never had a problem with 'discipline bloat', because it's so easy to say &quot;This is a Camarilla chronicle, standard disciplines only, please.&quot; Or any variant thereof. When you have 'linear' packages of powers like the original disciplines, it's effortless to make a distinction between the powers you want to see in the game and the powers of Sir Not-Appearing-in-This-Chronicle. At least for me, V5 style disciplines quickly lead to true discipline bloat, because every new power has to be shoved under one of the existing disciplines, and the GM has less control over what actually makes its way into the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T12:54:55-08:00","id":1468865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468860#post1468860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>1) Animalism - </b>Control animals and the nature of animals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>one Level 1 power have nothing to do with animals. It was an merit in prior editions: reconize someone as a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>10) Presence -</b> Control over the emotions of others. </div> </div> </div>Lingering Kiss gives buffs/penalties to the victim that has nothing to do with emotions. For example, you can literally increase someone's physical attributes. You can also make a person immune to presence effects, which sets up a mystical effect rather than an emotional effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7) Obfuscate - Misdirecting senses <b>to go unnoticed</b>. </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate 5 in v5 can make you Mystique. Became someone have nothing to do with go unnoticed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>6) Fortitude -</b> Greater resistance to damage physical or mental. </div> </div> </div>One of the new level 5 power give your bonus to general stats, can let you more quick, strong, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>2) Auspex - </b>Augmenting senses including attuning them to 'magic', or giving you extra-sensory perception. </div> </div> </div>One of the powers let you see the future/time travel to past once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>8) Oblivion - </b>Control/utilisation of the Abyss/Shadowlands and their manifestations in the skinlands. </div> </div> </div>One power let you change (protean?) your eyes to see ghosts (auspex?).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T13:05:46-08:00","id":1468866,"title":"","content":"A dozen. Call me a Noddist, but I prefer disciplines as applications of a nature that all kindred share. For example, I like Oblivion because there's an implication that it's based on a natural affinity that vampires have with destruction/anti-creation/nothingness/lower realms/MtAs entropy. If a bloodline or clan has the power to control something else, I expect an explanation about how they gained non-vampiric power, such as Lhiannan, Kiasyd or Ahrimanes, or that they aren't the same type of vampires, such as Wan Kuei. Even in the case of the former group, I find most older special disciplines a bit limited compared to common ones with alternative power choices.<br /> <br /> I'd consider replacing thin-blood alchemy with something like Mysteries of the Dragon. I'd also consider introducing means of interacting with adjacent and higher spirits, just because it could bring interesting aspects of WoD into VtM. Neither would be based on a dedicated discipline or be as flexible vampiric manipulation over animals, people, ghosts etc. for the reason I described in my first paragraph; it could be rather using Sense the Unseen to identify things visiting the world or their influence, if extraordinary, and another means to communicating with them, such as Feral Whispers with animal spirits. From there, it's a matter of bargaining, occult savvy, educated guesswork and existing covenants. I'm tempted by <i>Spiritus Sancti</i>, one of VtR's weird bloodline disciplines, which uses frenzy to commune with the spiritual, sometimes believed to be the divine, but that's mostly based on rule of cool (i.e. my own whim) and how it conveniently fits the Church of Caine's teachings.<br /> <br /> I add that there shouldn't be a limit on the number of discipline <i>powers</i> a character has; just charge xp for them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T13:30:14-08:00","id":1468870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468864#post1468864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, since you asked...<br /> <br /> My answer is thirty. Thirty disciplines. But only a third of them see anything approaching common usage in a given chronicle (the original ten disciplines). Roughly another third of them are for groups that operate mostly outside of normal Kindred society (the independents and the Sabbat). The last third of them are so rare that they are, in practical terms, NPC powers only (bloodline and inceptor disciplines, and so on).<br /> <br /> In other words, pretty much 2nd Edition by the book. There are no surprises here:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>The Original Ten</b><br /> Animalism<br /> Auspex<br /> Celerity<br /> Dominate<br /> Fortitude<br /> Obfuscate<br /> Potence<br /> Presence<br /> Protean<br /> Thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> <b>Independent Only</b><br /> Chimerstry<br /> Necromancy<br /> Quietus<br /> Serpentis<br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat Only</b><br /> Dementation<br /> Obtenebration<br /> Vicissitude<br /> <br /> <b>Odds and Ends</b><br /> Bardo<br /> Daimonion<br /> Dark Thaumaturgy<br /> Kineticism<br /> Melpominee<br /> Mytherceria<br /> Nihilistics<br /> Obeah<br /> Sanguinus<br /> Spiritus<br /> Temporis<br /> Thanatosis<br /> Visceratika</div></div> </div> </div><br /> I've never had a problem with 'discipline bloat', because it's so easy to say &quot;This is a Camarilla chronicle, standard disciplines only, please.&quot; Or any variant thereof. When you have 'linear' packages of powers like the original disciplines, it's effortless to make a distinction between the powers you want to see in the game and the powers of Sir Not-Appearing-in-This-Chronicle. At least for me, V5 style disciplines quickly lead to true discipline bloat, because every new power has to be shoved under one of the existing disciplines, and the GM has less control over what actually makes its way into the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its discipline bloat because you have a ton of useless disciplines that either will never get used or do things other disciplines already do. Getting rid of snowflake disciplines also ties in into V5 trying to make almost all clans fit for any chronicle, instead of limiting them due to their special discipline or metaplot reason. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468865#post1468865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one Level 1 power have nothing to do with animals. It was an merit in prior editions: reconize someone as a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulation of the beast and animal instincts is in animalism's purview<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lingering Kiss gives buffs/penalties to the victim that has nothing to do with emotions. For example, you can literally increase someone's physical attributes. You can also make a person immune to presence effects, which sets up a mystical effect rather than an emotional effect. </div> </div> </div>It only boosts one social attribute. It was adjusted a couple times. And it no longer has (don't remember if it ever had) this immunity effect. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obfuscate 5 in v5 can make you Mystique. Became someone have nothing to do with go unnoticed. </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate is more than just going unnoticed, its effectively sensory camouflage. At max level you can camouflage to look like someone else. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the new level 5 power give your bonus to general stats, can let you more quick, strong, etc. </div> </div> </div>One uses pain to draw more power from their blood, hence why the superhuman stats are limited by blood potency. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the powers let you see the future/time travel to past once. </div> </div> </div>Its magical scrying discipline. Allows you to hone your senses at early levels, to true scrying at later ones. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One power let you change (protean?) your eyes to see ghosts (auspex?). </div> </div> </div>You use the discipline that draws from the lands of the dead and beyond, to see the dead? Its not really out there. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T13:48:26-08:00","id":1468871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468865#post1468865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one Level 1 power have nothing to do with animals. It was an merit in prior editions: reconize someone as a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair point, I will correct my definition, Beasts works better in place of animals, 'The ability to control beasts and beings possessed of a bestial nature'. (Bestial nature, meaning things with any bestial temperament/instincts akin to a beast, so Werewolves and Vampires.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lingering Kiss gives buffs/penalties to the victim that has nothing to do with emotions. For example, you can literally increase someone's physical attributes. You can also make a person immune to presence effects, which sets up a mystical effect rather than an emotional effect. </div> </div> </div>Which iteration are we talking about, the V5 Companion? I'll grant this one gets a bit iffy (even the designers are clearly unsure what to do with it). I think this still falls under emotional control, <i>'The victim gains a bonus equal to half the user's Presence (round up) to on Social Attribute of their choice'. </i>To me this sounds like you impart a degree of your emotional manipulation to another, that's what's giving them the edge.<br /> <br /> I will grant this is one of those weird doesn't really fit powers. Fundamentally I think it'd be best-off cut and replaced with something else, but the rest of the powers hold to the definition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obfuscate 5 in v5 can make you Mystique. Became someone have nothing to do with go unnoticed. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I would say that still falls under the idea of going 'unnoticed' your true self, isn't seen you present a falsehood. You are still fundamentally deceiving the other person's senses. Again I think the powers fit, but will grant I might need to refine my definition. Perhaps 'The ability to fool the senses/sensors?', this covers Silence of Death, Unseen Passage, Ghost in the Machine, and powers like Mask of a Thousand Faces, as well as Fata Morgana, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the new level 5 power give your bonus to general stats, can let you more quick, strong, etc. </div> </div> </div>Prowess from Pain, is another odd one I will grant. I will note that it still fits in with the general <i>'Resistance to damage physical [...]'</i> part of my definition as it does mean <i>'the vampire no longer suffers and dice penalties from Health damage sustained, such as physical Impairment'. </i>The gaining additional dice aspect is weird. However, it is still reliant on you taking and surviving damage in order to grow stronger, which aligns with the <i>'Resistance to damage physical [...] </i>element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the powers let you see the future/time travel to past once. </div> </div> </div>That would fall under the area of <i>'extra-sensory perception'</i>. You are gaining the ability to perceive something beyond your standard sense, i.e. the future or the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One power let you change (protean?) your eyes to see ghosts (auspex?). </div> </div> </div>The change (i.e. the eyes going black) is flavour text. But to my mind that, seeing in the dark, and perceiving ghosts still falls under the definition I provided. <i>'</i><i>Control/utilisation'</i> which as a byproduct turns the eyes black, <i>'of the Abyss/Shadowlands' </i>understood to be the origin of or linked to darkness/shadow, <i>'and their manifestations in the skinlands' </i>manifestations such as darkness, shadows, and ghosts.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll grant there are some very rare edge-case powers that one might call edge-cases, but they're the exception rather than the rule.<br /> <br /> <b>The improved definitions:</b><br /> <b>1) Animalism - </b>The ability to control beasts and beings possessed of a bestial nature.<br /> <b>2) Auspex - </b>Augmenting senses including attuning them to 'magic', or giving you extra-sensory perception.<br /> <b>3) Blood Sorcery -</b> Vampiric magic (typically in the form of exerting 'control' over the blood), combining the schools of practice.<br /> <b>4) Celerity - </b>Speed and grace.<br /> <b>5) Dominate -</b> Direct mental control over others, including memories.<br /> <b>6) Fortitude -</b> Greater resistance to damage physical or mental.<br /> <b>7) Obfuscate -</b> The ability to fool or manipulate sensors/the senses.<br /> <b>8) Oblivion - </b>Control/utilisation of the Abyss/Shadowlands and their manifestations in the Skinlands.<br /> <b>9) Potence -</b> Greater strength channelled to various effects.<br /> <b>10) Presence -</b> Control over the emotions of others.<br /> <b>11) Protean - </b>Shape-changing and manipulating organic matter.<br /> <b>12) Thin-Blood Alchemy -</b> Altering the properties of Thin-Blood vitae with certain ingredients. <i>(The only one that I'm shakey on really, still feels like they just wanted to give something cool to the Thin-Bloods. It could just as easily have been another type of Blood Sorcery, predominantly used by Thin-Bloods and requiring their vitae.)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":25061,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","user":"Karos","date":".  Addendum. 11-25-2021, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T14:32:15-08:00","id":1468873,"title":"","content":"I like the original ten Disciplines of the seven Camarilla clans from the original corebooks. I use a combination of the original Dark Ages Mortis and Obtenbration as a replacement for those two in-clan disciplines. I made Quietus and Serpentis a form of Thaumaturgy. I don't use Chimestry or Viccistude at all. I gave Protean to the Tzimisce. I've never figured out how to use Ravnos so I'm still uncertain what to give them. I'd likely redo their entire Discipline line up. Those are everyone's in-clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I divide the Paths of Thaumaturgy into various groups. Some Paths are popularly known (like Movement of Mind, Lure of Flames, or Weather Control) and can be learned by almost anyone provided they have enough Occult knowledge and can find a mentor. There are a lot of Paths that are Tremere only, and some Paths are only known to specific chantries or factions within the Tremere. A Tremere must play the political game to learn those. Then there are Paths only known to the Setites, Assamites, or the Tremere anti-tribu. Some Paths are known to other groups/orders/factions/secret societies not based on clan. Certain Paths are openly known among the Sabbat - they were gifts given to them by House Goratrix as proof of goodwill when they defected.<br /> <br /> Then I have &quot;secret&quot; Disciplines only known to certain Kindred that are not &quot;in-clan&quot; for anyone. Necromancy and its Paths are those available to the Giovanni/Cappadocians/Samedi, certain members of the Sabbat on the Path of Death and the Soul, and a few other Kindred who study the dead and the netherworld. I allow the Cappadocians and their other lineages to purchase it for in-clan XP (just to be fair to players), but everyone else it would be out-of-clan. Bardo is a Discipline known only to the Children of Osiris (which is a sect and not a bloodline) and can only be purchased with out-of-clan XP. While Dominate is in-clan for Malkavians, <i>some</i> Sabbat Malkavians know Dementation (it is not the original Discipline for the Malkavians, but a secret mystery discovered by certain Sabbat Malkavians and is again out-of-clan). Dark Thaumaturgy obviously exists for Infernalist characters.<br /> <br /> I only use Bloodlines sparingly, and never liked the idea that the interesting thing about them is their unique Discipline. If I include them in a chronicle, it's because they and the mystery about them are to play an important role in the chronicle. If so, I'll make a decision then as to whether they actually have a unique/signature Discipline. The Salubri definitely exist in my chronicles, so both Obeah and Valeren exist as creations of Saulot. (I'm on the fence whether they should be an actual Discipline, a Path of Thaumaturgy, or something different). Gargoyles exist, but are not Kindred but monstrous constructs of the Tremere with powers whose game mechanics are the same as Disciplines, but they aren't actually Disciplines. At some point, the ritual that created them stopped working. The Blood Brothers do exist as a creation of the Sabbat so Sanguinus exists (and is limited to them). But the ritual to create them often fails so their numbers are limited. I haven't introduced any other Bloodlines in my chronicles so I am keeping it open whether they exist or not.<br /> <br /> I don't allow Inceptor Disciplines. Sorry Caitiffs and Thin-Bloods. Enjoy the suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T18:23:31-08:00","id":1468880,"title":"","content":"The only change I'm a little iffy on with the V5 disciplines is Oblivion. There's just such an obvious divide between the function of Obtenebration and Necromancy that it feels awkward to shove them both together. Personally I'd prefer to either keep them distinct. (One could maybe argue to shove the ceremonies in as a form of Blood Sorcery, but to me this would be a worse version of the Oblivion problem, I'd rather have Hecata with shadow tentacles than Hecata using Thaumaturgy after all.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T18:51:20-08:00","id":1468881,"title":"","content":"I have run games with just a handful of clans, and greatly reduced Discipline lists, I find most of the latter Clans/Disciplines unneeded. I too like Salubri more and more, but it's mostly because I drop Valeren for Potence on the Warriors, and turn healing of wounds and madness into a couple combo powers of Auspex/Fortitude and Auspex/Presence. They add a D&amp;D vibe, and I like the idea of a clan running around in pairs more often than not.<br /> <br /> I think Auspex, Dominate, and Presence could get merged if you really wanted to slim down the list maybe Aus 1, Dom 2&amp;3, Aus 4, then Pre 5 be the DAV level 6 passion. I think things like Necromancy/Obtenibration are places where 5th really slipped off the tracks trying to slim down the list.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24666\" data-vbnamecard=\"24666\">Ravian</a> yeah, got a phone call while typing, completely agree Oblivion really falls short of making sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 11-25-2021, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T04:36:25-08:00","id":1468913,"title":"","content":"I think the question itself is problematic by being framed without consideration to how Disciplines work in the first place. Which brings us the problem of each one answering more with preferred edition or house-rule instead of putting the list they use.<br /> <br /> My preferred take is Requiem 2nd editions' list. A limited number of powers with broad applications and versatile mechanics. I particularly love their work with Auspex and Protean. And on top of that Devotions, a simple rule to add new powers without building an entire new Discipline from scratch.<br /> <br /> But a list of Disciplines I make based on those rules simply won't work in a game using any edition's VtM rules for Disciplines. The ideal list pretty much depends on the base rule of how those things will work in the end.<br /> <br /> Without a rule similar to Devotions it is really hard to justify trimming down the number of Disciplines, because sooner or later you'll want a character with a power that doesn't quite fits with what you already have. Of course, you can take the simplest route of banning them from your game altogether and stick to it, but I don't find it a positive framework to start from as Storyteller. And yes, they are gimmicky powers. This isn't a problem at all, gimmicks are useful plot devices, for major, minor and personal plots.<br /> <br /> Combo Disciplines, now Amalgams, have existed to cover that for some time now. But they present problems that still keeps them from working properly. The first is the heft requisite for a power that isn't always that powerful and you may want to give it to an inexperienced character, PC or NPC. Devotions only have to require a single Discipline.<br /> <br /> Going with V1-20 take on Disciplines, with very strictly defined chain of powers and Combos being few and little known, it is unavoidable to have a bazillion gimmicky Disciplines. If that's the route, then I'm staying with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1190_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1190\" data-vbnamecard=\"1190\">Elphilm</a> on that one. It is not Discipline bloat, you still have only 10 that you need to use with any regularity. Everything else is color for particular characters and are readily available on the books, why bother reinventing the wheel? The setting works just fine as is (in this regard).<br /> <br /> <b>V5 changes little on the problem</b>. You still have the same number of powers (give or take few) and they still take their specific slots in your character sheet. They are just organized differently. This new organization makes sense? Yes, it does. Barely, but it does. And it does solve problems when entire Disciplines existed only because of a couple key powers, but it also keep the particular powers just as unnecessarily specific as always, if not more.<br /> <br /> Yet, the damn slots <b>are</b> a problem that makes little sense. Forcing a character to forever forfeit all other options when choosing a power for a given slot is a strange design decision I still don't understand. On top of that, Amalgams are more visible, which is a plus, but they take out slots, which is a huge down. So I'd it's a solid draw between the two options, pre and post V5.<br /> <br /> On the end of the day, the 10 original Disciplines are a pretty solid basis, you don't strictly need anything else, we just need a mechanic to deal with variations and novelties, as they need a place. VtM lacks that. And putting Necromancy into Oblivion is plain bad, seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T11:55:46-08:00","id":1468928,"title":"","content":"Part of the issue with the v5's 10 (outside of oblivion being both mechanically and lore wise a hot garbage fire.) Is it's self defeating in its approach, you can see a sort of subtle evolution already occurring where former disciplines are being hammered into them. Slowly Re creating the complexity and bloat which previous editions are accused of having, this becomes becomes especially absurd as loresheet effectively become a supplementary range of psuado mystic powers which are disciplines while pretending not to be (eg harbingers of Ashurs mask system.)<br /> The ultimate issue is if v5 produces more written books more powers will emerge so the question becomes redundant as each of the 10/ loresheets are expected to carry multiple powers formally represented by disciplines to the point of absurdity....as has already been achieved with Oblivion which is at best two disciplines which don't mesh if I'm being nice and more accurately 2 disciplines and several necromantic/mortis paths. I suspect this is how they will all turn out as v5 grinds on.<br /> <br /> But back to the question:no idea, as many as needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-26-2021, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T13:02:19-08:00","id":1468929,"title":"","content":"As many as needed. If thats 10, 20 or 50 then so be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T13:51:20-08:00","id":1468932,"title":"","content":"I wish they'd have about 13 Disciplines and the ability to buy unlimited numbers of Combo Disciplines and Powers at every level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T16:09:13-08:00","id":1468934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468932#post1468932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish they'd have about 13 Disciplines and the ability to buy unlimited numbers of Combo Disciplines and Powers at every level.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... the VtR approach?<br /> <br /> I'm being a bit facetious here, but VtR has 13 core Disciplines, and unlimited Devotions (either for combo Discipline powers, or alternate powers), and in 2e has moved away from lots of custom Disciplines for Bloodlines (even if left the option open). The Blasphemies and Sacrements VtR supplement lets you expand Cruac/Theban Sorcery to cover other forms of blood sorcery and actually has rule for making your own rituals (whether purely OOC, or as an IC thing to make those Disciplines more flexible).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T16:52:59-08:00","id":1468935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468934#post1468934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... the VtR approach?<br /> <br /> I'm being a bit facetious here, but VtR has 13 core Disciplines, and unlimited Devotions (either for combo Discipline powers, or alternate powers), and in 2e has moved away from lots of custom Disciplines for Bloodlines (even if left the option open). The Blasphemies and Sacrements VtR supplement lets you expand Cruac/Theban Sorcery to cover other forms of blood sorcery and actually has rule for making your own rituals (whether purely OOC, or as an IC thing to make those Disciplines more flexible).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I think the biggest issues right now for Disciplines are that you have a limit on how many powers you can have and the Limit to Level 5.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T17:06:50-08:00","id":1468936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468932#post1468932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish they'd have about 13 Disciplines and the ability to buy unlimited numbers of Combo Disciplines and Powers at every level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually enjoy the idea of Devotions (combo discipline powers) in Masquerade. I was in the past mostly able to turn the bulk of Dementation into powers built off of Auspex, Dominate, and Obfuscate. <br /> <br /> I've fiddled with the idea of Spiritus (the Ahrimanes' power) as Devotions of Auspex, Animalism, and Protean, but since I almost never use that bloodline, I've never really finished it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T23:04:45-08:00","id":1468943,"title":"","content":"Devotions let you have alternate powers for each level, let you have combo powers if you want, and since they may be exceptionally powerful then have requisites like Blood Potency 6+, they cover the Elder/Methuselah powers without the need for technically saying that you have more than 5 dots in the Discipline.<br /> <br /> Without the limit on powers the only thing the V5 Disciplines would lack in this regard would be XP adjustment for particularly powerful effects, but that's a minor loss. I still ave problems with the powers themselves being more restrict and will probably just take the cue of the change in rules to port Requiem's Disciplines entirely.<br /> <br /> But yeah. With a decent Devotion-like rule to cover variety, something between 10 to 13 Disciplines is enough. Without it, then just let there be a bazillion, you just need a reference document for the extras and it isn't as hard to deal with as it used to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T00:08:42-08:00","id":1468946,"title":"","content":"5.<br /> <br /> And Blood Magic shouldn\u2019t be a thing at all, at least not in the way it\u2019s been presented in any of the editions. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T01:17:58-08:00","id":1468953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468946#post1468946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5.<br /> <br /> And Blood Magic shouldn\u2019t be a thing at all, at least not in the way it\u2019s been presented in any of the editions.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? Explain how this works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T01:55:40-08:00","id":1468957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468929#post1468929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As many as needed. If thats 10, 20 or 50 then so be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the correct answer.<br /> <br /> Not everyone is going to use every Discipline. This is fine. They just need to exist for when a Storyteller or Player wants to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T01:57:49-08:00","id":1468958,"title":"","content":"I must admit I'm curious what preventative measures people would propose to prevent the v5 discipline cap becoming redundant as the 10 get flooded with increasing numbers of alternative/combo powers would produce simular issues to a large number of disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-27-2021, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T04:15:32-08:00","id":1468969,"title":"","content":"I'm in agreement with Elphilim here. 10 original ones, although !'ll let a player snag the occasional odd one for a really good backstory or good play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T06:46:22-08:00","id":1468977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468946#post1468946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5.<br /> <br /> And Blood Magic shouldn\u2019t be a thing at all, at least not in the way it\u2019s been presented in any of the editions.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am guessing the three physical disciplines are in the 5, just curious what the other two are. Without Obfuscate there is less need for Auspex, are you going classic? Protean and Dominate? Some kind of catch all 2 that combine multiple disciplines? I have often nuked Blood Magic myself, so just wondering where your at. I wouldn't think Animalism makes the cut if there are only 2 slots left after Celerity, Fortitude, Potence.<br /> <br /> When I thought about a Vampire Diaries world game it's pretty clear newborn vampires start with 3 in Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude, and Potence on the TV show. Protean was used in the books and the pilot episode.<br /> <br /> I think if you limit the disciplines to 5, either you cut down the number of clans, or you really lean into the Clan flaws being what separates them. If you are going that small I would just give all vampires the same weaknesses, and let sects be the big factor. Not really VTM, but could be a really fun chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T07:14:14-08:00","id":1468979,"title":"","content":"The essential problem I've always had with the blood sorcery disciplines is that selling books with more blood sorcery powers over the course of an expansion is always part of the business model. If I were still actively storytelling, I'd crack down with a house rule that each path is a separate discipline and each ritual is an amalgam power with a second discipline as a requirement. It's all from the power in the blood, so it works by the same rules as the rest of the powers in the blood. Pay the experience costs if you want to be a Halliwell sister instead of a vampire.<br /> <br /> Then restat the thaumaturge NPC's accordingly. The Tremere contact doesn't know the ritual that's needed, so he reaches out and trades favors with a specialist within the clan who can perform it. Presto, the entire wizard clan just became more interesting and nuanced then they are when every NPC can cast every spell in the game.<br /> <br /> This unfortunately blows up the number of disciplines in the game, but it could be mitigated by merging the different cultural schools of blood sorcery and cutting the redundancies, as Aleph suggests in the second post in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T08:54:06-08:00","id":1468990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468958#post1468958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit I'm curious what preventative measures people would propose to prevent the v5 discipline cap becoming redundant as the 10 get flooded with increasing numbers of alternative/combo powers would produce simular issues to a large number of disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Planning the game's design? Potence hasn't gotten a single extra power since release for example. It's not really an apt comparison anyway, having extra options to choose from isn't bad, problem is when it gets excessive and redundant, this way you don't need 5+ powers just to have an interesting one.<br /> <br /> Cutting down on powers isn't the only benefit as well, its about giving more player options, this way you don't have super specific disciplines that are barely used. By putting those powers at standard disciplines, it opens up a lot of option for player characters to play different concepts more easily without having to play a bloodline that only exists to justify its silly discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T09:02:01-08:00","id":1468991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468990#post1468990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Planning the game's design? Potence hasn't gotten a single extra power since release for example. It's not really an apt comparison anyway, having extra options to choose from isn't bad, problem is when it gets excessive and redundant, this way you don't need 5+ powers just to have an interesting one.<br /> <br /> Cutting down on powers isn't the only benefit as well, its about giving more player options, this way you don't have super specific disciplines that are barely used. By putting those powers at standard disciplines, it opens up a lot of option for player characters to play different concepts more easily without having to play a bloodline that only exists to justify its silly discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a valid reply but you don't seem on the expand the powers of the 10 camp with combo powers and multiple choices per level my question is more directed at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-27-2021, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T09:31:47-08:00","id":1468994,"title":"","content":"I see.<br /> <br /> On the subject of multiple choices per level, it's a hard thing to balance. I think it shouldn't be something immediately available, but some long term goal. Being able to purchase additional powers after rank 5 at standard costs works more or less, though I'd like to tie it to Blood Potency as well (Maybe up to half your blood potency?). It'd be less efficient than usual as you don't gain extra dots, but that would give it more balance. Its generally the rule I use when making SPCs, so that only the few true elders (and Methuseleahs if I ever use one) get extra powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T11:10:43-08:00","id":1469004,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it the ideal of the 10 disciplines speaks more to modern societies subconscious desire to return to the idealised simpler states of play rather than any inherent merit. You may as well argue for only roughly 4 disciplines- morphic, mental, physical, mystical and cram all the powers into that to reach the logical conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T14:43:35-08:00","id":1469022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468990#post1468990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Planning the game's design? Potence hasn't gotten a single extra power since release for example. It's not really an apt comparison anyway, having extra options to choose from isn't bad, problem is when it gets excessive and redundant, this way you don't need 5+ powers just to have an interesting one.<br /> <br /> Cutting down on powers isn't the only benefit as well, its about giving more player options, this way you don't have super specific disciplines that are barely used. By putting those powers at standard disciplines, it opens up a lot of option for player characters to play different concepts more easily without having to play a bloodline that only exists to justify its silly discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - Planning design won't change the simple fact that new powers will be designed. Although I do agree that V5's method reduces the need for making them in packets of 5, which <i><b>is</b></i> a plus;<br /> <br /> 2 - There is certainly some redundancy in pre-V5 Disciplines due to the 5-pack aspect, but I hardly think they're excessive. How you define it? At no point the game presses you into using more than the 10 standard, 12 if you want heavy Sabbat presence. Everything else is dependent on you wanting to use their far more specific groups to begin with;<br /> <br /> 3 - Having more player options to build individual versions of a Discipline is certainly a plus. But talking about excess from one method while defending another that effectively and on design increases the amount of powers at the players' disposal on a regular basis is complicated. By pre-V5 you have no need to allow more than 10 discipline, to a total of 50 structured powers. By V5 you have at least twice as much powers, with more intricate combinations;<br /> <br /> 4 - No bloodline to my knowledge exists solely to justify a Discipline. Although I certainly can't say they share the same quality of writing, applicability on play or anything else, every bloodlne was designed on its own merits and their own Disciplines exist to better represent their particularities instead of them existing for the Discipline's sake.<br /> <br /> You have fair points about this take on Disciplines over others, but keep your arguments from spilling into pure offense against other editions.<br /> <br /> As for my opinion on taking more powers of the same level in a Discipline in V5, I don't think any extra requisite should be necessary. Do it at the normal price for that level, doing so doesn't increase your dot rating, the end. This isn't as big a deal as it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T16:26:53-08:00","id":1469037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469022#post1469022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 - No bloodline to my knowledge exists solely to justify a Discipline. Although I certainly can't say they share the same quality of writing, applicability on play or anything else, every bloodlne was designed on its own merits and their own Disciplines exist to better represent their particularities instead of them existing for the Discipline's sake.<br /> <br /> You have fair points about this take on Disciplines over others, but keep your arguments from spilling into pure offense against other editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>My general distaste for many bloodlines did slip through. But some bloodlines do feel really hollow if you take their discipline away. The Trujah are the low hanging fruit, but are the prime example, without Temporis they are a 180 on the Brujah Stereotype. Only difference between them and the main clan being that they are solely nerds while the main clan has variety. Which I think weakens the main Brujah clan a lot. <br /> <br /> Daughters of Cacophony is another, remove their singing discipline and they are Toreadors that are focused solely on singing or Malkavians whose bane is Magic Tinnitus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469022#post1469022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my opinion on taking more powers of the same level in a Discipline in V5, I don't think any extra requisite should be necessary. Do it at the normal price for that level, doing so doesn't increase your dot rating, the end. This isn't as big a deal as it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not extremely strong in general, but some disciplines get really stronger, Dominate, Obfuscate and Fortitude especially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T17:04:48-08:00","id":1469045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468953#post1468953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? Explain how this works?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<span style=\"color:#000000\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Won't let me post with less than 10 words, so... The Clan Tremere were a poor and misguided attempt on Rein\u2022Hagen's part to either cross-pollinate players between <i>Vampire</i> and <i>Ars Magica</i>, or an unnecessary nod to his time on the latter. The only tenuous mythological link to &quot;vampire wizards&quot; is a mention that Dracula studied at the Scholomance, but even that was a theory by the character of Van Helsing. And blood magic should be about blood - not flinging fireballs, or budget telekinesis, or wannbe-Obtenebration by a bunch of poor-mans' Raistlins. The game would only have benefited from the omission of the Tremere in its initial development. </div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 11-27-2021, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T17:25:43-08:00","id":1469049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468977#post1468977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am guessing the three physical disciplines are in the 5, just curious what the other two are.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the physical Disciplines can be modeled by reducing difficulty, granting automatic successes, and so on. Arguably, spending Blood to increase physical traits is just as good compared to any of the physical Disciplines. There should be:<br /> <br /> \u2022Protean (encompassing Vicissitude, Serpentis, really any Discipline that transfigures one's self)<br /> \u2022Dominate (and all related mental trickery like Dementation, Obfuscate, the first few levels of Chimerstry (and the later levels shouldn't even be allowed, because where the hell does <i>spontaneous</i> <i>origination</i> of material goods fall in vampire myth?) Melpominee - which is just Dementation with singing; etc.)<br /> \u2022Auspex<br /> \u2022Animalism<br /> \u2022Presence if you have to, even though it's really just more Charisma dice<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 11-27-2021, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T20:17:56-08:00","id":1469065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469045#post1469045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Won't let me post with less than 10 words, so... The Clan Tremere are a poor and misguided attempt on Rein\u2022Hagen's part to either cross-pollinate players between <i>Vampire</i> and <i>Ars Magica</i>, or an unnecessary nod to his time on the latter. The only tenuous mythological link to &quot;vampire wizards&quot; is a mention that Dracula studied at the Scholomance, but even that was a theory by the character of Van Helsing. And blood magic should be about blood - not flinging fireballs, or budget telekinesis, or wannbe-Obtenebration by a bunch of poor-mans' Raistlins. The game would only have benefited from the omission of the Tremere in its initial development.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't post with most of your text invisible.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T21:14:36-08:00","id":1469067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469065#post1469065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't post with most of your text invisible.</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Most? So does that mean it's okay to post with <i>all</i> of the text invisible? :P</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T00:23:13-08:00","id":1469075,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T06:30:38-08:00","id":1469093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469037#post1469037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general distaste for many bloodlines did slip through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that and have my own opinions on them, too. But even those are not a case of being bad because they exist exist for the Disciplines. It is just that their concepts are as... arguable... as it gets on their own.<br /> <br /> To take on those examples, the <i>Trujah</i> exist first and foremost to be this big secret, as a part of the whole <i>True Black Hand</i> shenanigans. Temporis is pretty much an afterthought to that. I'm not very fond of them either, although I learned to accept and use them.<br /> <br /> And the Daughters, they always seemed to me quite literally an exercise on bloodline creation, a sample of what you can make with the concept to have a new option in your game without changing many things. They're like vanilla for bloodlines, the most neutral use of the concept possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469037#post1469037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not extremely strong in general, but some disciplines get really stronger, Dominate, Obfuscate and Fortitude especially.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I would have to look at them more thoroughly to be sure, but it could be the case on giving the problem ones a little more restriction instead of doing that to every Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T09:37:57-08:00","id":1469102,"title":"","content":"The Blood Brothers, Gargoyles, Lamia, Samedi, Maeghar and Baali are all <i>fucking awesome</i>. (if you ignore a few shitty texts) <br /> Most are decent. I quite like the variants of the big clans that don't stand apart too much. Lineage should be more than just how many people separate you from an antideluvian. <br /> <br /> The Ahrimanes, TrBr, Evil angles or whatever, Kiasyd... there's more than a few iffy things there. <br /> <br /> A Vampire wrapped around their specialist discipline isn't a problem. Several of the Big Clans frequently have members than do that, and it' not a problem. Thaumaturgy, Vicissitude, Obtenebration, Protean, Obfuscate...<br /> Bloodline are a nice curveball for when your players have slain their 9th Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T09:38:22-08:00","id":1469103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469045#post1469045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Won't let me post with less than 10 words, so... The Clan Tremere were a poor and misguided attempt on Rein\u2022Hagen's part to either cross-pollinate players between <i>Vampire</i> and <i>Ars Magica</i>, or an unnecessary nod to his time on the latter. The only tenuous mythological link to &quot;vampire wizards&quot; is a mention that Dracula studied at the Scholomance, but even that was a theory by the character of Van Helsing. And blood magic should be about blood - not flinging fireballs, or budget telekinesis, or wannbe-Obtenebration by a bunch of poor-mans' Raistlins. The game would only have benefited from the omission of the Tremere in its initial development.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't a very good line of reasoning. Vampires and quasi vampires have a long historical links with magic in folklore of many culture. To.the point theirs quite a lot of overlap between witchcraft and vampirism is slacks folklore. While hermetic magic isn't really linked with then, the idea of vampires has a lot of overlap with taboo magics. So dracula is hardly the only precedence <br /> <br /> As for 'Blood magic' its important to distinguish between fuel vs effect. While using blood as a method to produce effects is historically common it doesn't typically manifest itself as the blood physically doing something that's a pretty new idea. So it's perfectly logical to use the blood 'mana' to produce a fireball. Afterall it'd be silly if mages could only fire loafs of bread or apple juice from their hands <br /> <br /> Finally the Tremere are a popular clan with a rich and interesting history which people enjoy playing. That alone justifies them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-28-2021, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T09:47:00-08:00","id":1469104,"title":"","content":"Realtalk:<br /> I think Tremere have magic the way they do because the creators were interested in Hermeticism and the idea that we're all imperfect beings standing below some divine truth, waiting for the day where we can improve ourselves and climb back into the light and become one with The Almighty/TheUniverse/WhatThePlayeresWant. Vampires haven't chosen to be damned, so they have just as much a shot at enlightenment as ordinary folk. Hermetic magic is essentially an exercise in self improvement that isn't denied to vampires because... vampires do still have souls.<br /> Settites later reinforce this with Gnosticism. They're like the Anti-Tremere with very similar ideas and a very different perspective.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cutting the magic out would shit on what Vampire's all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T10:04:13-08:00","id":1469106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469104#post1469104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realtalk:<br /> I think Tremere have magic the way they do because the creators were interested in Hermeticism and the idea that we're all imperfect beings standing below some divine truth, waiting for the day where we can improve ourselves and climb back into the light and become one with The Almighty/TheUniverse/WhatThePlayeresWant. Vampires haven't chosen to be damned, so they have just as much a shot at enlightenment as ordinary folk. Hermetic magic is essentially an exercise in self improvement that isn't denied to vampires because... vampires do still have souls.<br /> Settites later reinforce this with Gnosticism. They're like the Anti-Tremere with very similar ideas and a very different perspective.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cutting the magic out would shit on what Vampire's all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I always considered pretty much all the vampire magics as hedge magic filtered/enhanced/corrupted through the curse with strong sympathetic links with death and blood ensuring certain types of magic came more naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T11:57:31-08:00","id":1469109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469103#post1469103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't a very good line of reasoning. Vampires and quasi vampires have a long historical links with magic in folklore of many culture. To.the point theirs quite a lot of overlap between witchcraft and vampirism is slacks folklore. <b>While hermetic magic isn't really linked with then,</b> the idea of vampires has a lot of overlap with taboo magics. So dracula is hardly the only precedence</div> </div> </div> </div>I have emboldened the part of your argument that enforces my statement. Witchcraft akin to <i>hedge magic</i> has been associated with vampires, not rigid hierarchical structures like The Order of Hermes. Clan Tremere should be closer to the Verbena.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for 'Blood magic' its important to distinguish between fuel vs effect. While using blood as a method to produce effects is historically common it doesn't typically manifest itself as the blood physically doing something that's a pretty new idea. So it's perfectly logical to use the blood 'mana' to produce a fireball. Afterall it'd be silly if mages could only fire loafs of bread or apple juice from their hands </div> </div> </div>And that's the issue. Aside from one Path and a handful of rituals, Thaumaturgy <i>doesn't involve blood at all</i>.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally the Tremere are a popular clan with a rich and interesting history which people enjoy playing. That alone justifies them. </div> </div> </div>That is <i>one</i> opinion. Here's some other popular opinions. Note that none of them are mine, but have been expressed previously on this forum: 1) Vampire mages don't fit in a gothic-punk personal horror setting; 2) Thaumaturgy is (overpowered/watered down/insert your own gripe here); 3) Blood magics are a cash cow money grab in supplements and ruined the game; etc,. My favorite opinion is to paraphrase Steve Allen: Comedy is tragedy plus time, so Clan Tremere are a bunch of clowns.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T12:00:06-08:00","id":1469110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469109#post1469109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have emboldened the part of your argument that enforces my statement. Witchcraft akin to <i>hedge magic</i> has been associated with vampires, not rigid hierarchical structures like The Order of Hermes. Clan Tremere should be closer to the Verbena.<br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>So would you include Cruac, perhaps in a simplified form, but not Theban Sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T12:02:34-08:00","id":1469111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469104#post1469104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cutting the magic out would shit on what Vampire's all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely disagree, and anecdotally, so does the last decade of my gaming experience.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T12:09:46-08:00","id":1469113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469110#post1469110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would you include Cruac, perhaps in a simplified form, but not Theban Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not familiar with VtR and what those are, but after a quick glimpse at the wiki, sure, yeah. Cr\u00faac seems much more in-line with actual blood magics.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T13:05:48-08:00","id":1469117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469109#post1469109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have emboldened the part of your argument that enforces my statement. Witchcraft akin to <i>hedge magic</i> has been associated with vampires, not rigid hierarchical structures like The Order of Hermes. Clan Tremere should be closer to the Verbena.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correct but the jump isnt that dramatic a jump is it? we've already established a link between magic and vampires so the faustian rites which created the Tremere with the sinister <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">arts they do now</span></span></span> arnt that un-vampiric are they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's the issue. Aside from one Path and a handful of rituals, Thaumaturgy <i>doesn't involve blood at all</i>. </div> </div> </div>That's not strictly speaking true, since all paths are fuelled by blood arnt they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is <i>one</i> opinion. Here's some other popular opinions. Note that none of them are mine, but have been expressed previously on this forum: 1) Vampire mages don't fit in a gothic-punk personal horror setting; 2) Thaumaturgy is (overpowered/watered down/insert your own gripe here); 3) Blood magics are a cash cow money grab in supplements and ruined the game; etc,. My favorite opinion is to paraphrase Steve Allen: Comedy is tragedy plus time, so Clan Tremere are a bunch of clowns. </div> </div> </div>No it's a fact, unless you're arguing that the Tremere arn't a popular choice?<br /> <br /> 1) Sinister Cabals of Blood sorcerors engaging in vile rites while re-enforcing a corrupt status quo slowly sapping the human spirit in an dystopian urban setting isnt gothic punk?<br /> 2) I've personally never really found any of the disciplines particularly balanced. singling out thaumaturgy always seemed odd for a number of reasons. If you're going to powergame their are quicker cheaper more efficient options and if they're underpowered why would I care if you're having fun?<br /> 3)I don't really think the game was ever 'ruined' but I'd point more to economic trends and internal issues in WW than over indulgant path flooding. I honestly don't think I've even seen a path which isnt either core or guide to played except path of shadows as a plot point for an npc.<br /> If it's not your opinions but others I'd recommend more diverse perspectives for a more even tempered mindsets as a rule of thumb I try to pick perspectives which contradict mine or plays devils advocate. Hence why I enjoy this discussion over someone who could remind me how much I think v5's lore is trash.<br /> <br /> Quotation, n: The act of repeating erroneously the words of another.\u201d<br /> \u2015 Ambrose Bierce, <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/865289\" target=\"_blank\">The Unabridged Devil's Dictionary</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-28-2021, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T13:55:52-08:00","id":1469123,"title":"","content":"The #2 opinion is also a lot more nuanced in a fashion that doesn't support just dumping any vampire sorcery that isn't &quot;bloody&quot; enough (because you could replicate all the mechanical gripes with Thaumaturgy in Cruac if you implemented it with the same issues).<br /> <br /> 1) A big issue is that the secondary paths are all cheaper in XP costs. As far as &quot;powergaming&quot; goes in all this, it makes Thaumaturgy the best all-round option. It might not be as good as a specialist in one area, but it's the fastest/cheapest way to be good in lots of areas. Having Thaumaurgy (or any other blood sorcery) in-clan means raising your primary Path is also much easier to do. Not every &quot;powergamer&quot; problem is mechanics where you min-max into being the ultimate hammer, and then try to solve everything in the game as if it's a nail. There's also the Linear Warrior Quadratic Wizard concept (a D&amp;D-ism, so this is not some VtM specific issue) where casters out-shine non-casters over time due increasing both versatility and effectiveness simultaneously where non-casters can only advance one category at a time.<br /> <br /> 2) This leads to a second issue where Thaumaturgy (but not all blood sorcery in VtM) has the same roll for every path activation. You max out one dice-pool, and you've maxed out activating every path; and rituals only add a second dice-pool which due to char-gen issues is easy to max separately. This increases the perceived issues with #1, but is a separate mechanical gripe that is a problem for people on its own (esp. people that don't like how it was clearly done to keep Thaumaturgy the &quot;best&quot; blood magic even as the game added more practices in).<br /> <br /> 3) Rituals are an unlimited source of additional powers; nobody else gets to just learn new powers for free like that (V5 added XP costs to these, but kept the overall problem by making amalgams count towards your total power cap while rituals don't). This furthers the gripes even more because, again, its the &quot;one stop shop&quot; effect. Why bother trying to find a Protean user so you can learn Protean 1 and 2, or all that XP for the Burning Hand combo Discipline, when you can learn a ritual to get a magical agg dealing sword for no XP, while your XP goes to other things other than access to agg damage non-bite attacks?<br /> <br /> None of this though, is a case for, &quot;the Tremere and/or Thaumaturgy shouldn't exist,&quot; because all of that is fixable. The XP price for secondary paths is just a number (or there's the VtR method where all of it is ritual magic and there's no need for paths and players have to pick XP on the Discipline to get more potent at magic, or XP on rituals to do more things with it). VtM introduced other models for activation rolls so characters can't master casting significantly more easily than mastering the multiple activation rolls for many core Disciplines. Rituals can be given XP costs in pre-V5, or V5 can unblock amalgams so rituals don't feel cheesy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T14:13:02-08:00","id":1469125,"title":"","content":"The other way to solve the matter of Rituals is to keep them free, but decouple it from the Thaumaturgy Discipline itself. Letting anyone attempt to cast it, so long as they know how. Anyone could, with research and the proper materials, do magic. It's just that groups like the Tremere hoard knowledge so jealously.<br /> <br /> Of course, that also undermines the conception of Sorcery as something that requires years of study and understanding in order to grasp even on an elementary level. Not to mention, without being tied to a linear progression you have to buy with XP, it's harder to prevent characters from just bum-rushing high level Rituals. (Other than the ST putting up barriers to access, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T14:13:51-08:00","id":1469126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469117#post1469117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct but the jump isnt that dramatic a jump is it? we've already established a link between magic and vampires so the faustian rites which created the Tremere with the sinister arts they do now arnt that un-vampiric are they?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've also established a link that vampires avoid sunlight, but making them sparkle instead of burst into ash seems to have upset the &quot;purists,&quot; so let's not engage in that slippery slope. Let's also agree not to get into semantic debates that Thaumaturgy actually means &quot;miracle-working,&quot; since it does fall under the category of Blood Sorcery.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not strictly speaking true, since all paths are fuelled by blood arnt they? </div> </div> </div>Are they? Because nowhere in the game's mechanics is this enforced. Path of Blood doesn't fuel <i>anything</i>. There's barely a narrative hand-wave, the text claiming that Clan Tremere can do all this cool stuff because they studied vitae after they couldn't tap quintessence anymore. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No it's a fact, unless you're arguing that the Tremere arn't a popular choice? </div> </div> </div>I'm not for or against their popularity; rather, I'm against the idea of this unequivocal fact when there is at least one person who disagrees entirely. That's the problem with art - it's open to interpretation; there can be no objective &quot;fact&quot; when I find Clan Tremere's &quot;rich and interesting history&quot; to be trite and unnecessary.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's not your opinions but others I'd recommend more diverse perspectives for a more even tempered mindsets as a rule of thumb I try to pick perspectives which contradict mine or plays devils advocate. Hence why enjoy this discussion over someone who could remind me how much I think v5's lore is trash. </div> </div> </div>The popular opinion <b>is</b> the one that contradicts mine; the majority of casual players don't even have an opinion on this. It takes an echo chamber like ours to really get involved in these debates (have you seen the other social media pages? None of them are as in-depth as us. We're fanatics).<br /> <br /> We'll probably just end up talking in circles, so I'll end with this: I know Clan Tremere is popular and people like playing vampire wizards, so I haven't eliminated them completely from my games like I want. I have used something like a proto-V5 loresheet that fundamentally alters the Tremere, because if your ass belongs to the Pyramid, then <i><b>your ass belongs to the Pyramid</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T14:27:53-08:00","id":1469127,"title":"","content":"I personally think that keeping Thaumaturgy Out of Clan for everyone solves everything I could reasonably have against it or the Tremere. As a clan of hermetic vampires I think their concept work, magic or not. As an extraneous thing that any character can learn if and when the ST presents an opportunity to them, Thaumaturgy works.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar408_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"408\" data-vbnamecard=\"408\">nothing</a>'s take is valid. Taking Thaumaturgy out of the game don't really hurt it that much and no one's required to like the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T17:11:42-08:00","id":1469134,"title":"","content":"At some point I decided to start treating the Daughters of Cacophony as being one of the signs/harbingers of Gehenna and the Final Nights, seeming to appear from nowhere around 150 to 250 years ago and tending to have bad fortune follow in their wake. Because Revised edition made Performance a main ability in place of Music and tied Melpominee to it instead of Music or Singing, and because I'm weirdly contrary by nature, I started taking a very broad interpretation of what counted as vocal performance, resulting in members who were Vaudeville ventriloquists, slightly cultist motivational speakers, and rabble-rousing street activist riot grrls, as well as tangential ideas like fey-struck anthropologist song-catchers and juke joint hoodoo practitioners, in addition to the more conventional film noir chanteuses, black metal witches, and hip hop divas. I interpret their weakness as being personalized and attuned to their concept/background, but with a lot of dark and disturbing undertones. (The Vaudevillian hearing old piano music and other period style works that tend to have an underlying sense of menace and madness, the anthropologist hearing &quot;fairy music&quot; tied to which ever culture she specializes in, and the hip hop diva her own personal soundtrack singing her praises and threatening her enemies, as examples.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T17:52:18-08:00","id":1469135,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469126#post1469126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've also established a link that vampires avoid sunlight, but making them sparkle instead of burst into ash seems to have upset the &quot;purists,&quot; so let's not engage in that slippery slope. Let's also agree not to get into semantic debates that Thaumaturgy actually means &quot;miracle-working,&quot; since it does fall under the category of Blood Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I never really lost much sleep over teenage romance novels so didnt really have a problem with twlight but I'm not sure using sinister magics to become a vampire and then a clan discipline is much of a slippery slope. more of an an logical incline. I havnt really commented on semantics one way or another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they? Because nowhere in the game's mechanics is this enforced. Path of Blood doesn't fuel <i>anything</i>. There's barely a narrative hand-wave, the text claiming that Clan Tremere can do all this cool stuff because they studied vitae after they couldn't tap quintessence anymore. </div> </div> </div>Well...yes but I said fuelled by blood not fuelled by the path of blood. all thaumaturgical path require blood to work so are implicitly blood magics right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not for or against their popularity; rather, I'm against the idea of this unequivocal fact when there is at least one person who disagrees entirely. That's the problem with art - it's open to interpretation; there can be no objective &quot;fact&quot; when I find Clan Tremere's &quot;rich and interesting history&quot; to be trite and unnecessary. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not arguing that my observation is that the Tremere are a popular play option and this justifies them as a valid play choice so to argue the game would have benefited from the absence is incorrect as players have directly benefited from it. Think of it this way-If I don't think a light fiction book is very a good how would the world be improved by it's absence if others enjoyed it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The popular opinion <b>is</b> the one that contradicts mine; the majority of casual players don't even have an opinion on this. It takes an echo chamber like ours to really get involved in these debates (have you seen the other social media pages? None of them are as indepth as us. We're fanatics). </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It would genuinely surprise me if casuals players would support the removal of clan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We'll probably just end up talking in circles, so I'll end with this: I know Clan Tremere is popular and people like playing vampire wizards, so I haven't eliminated them completely from my games like I want. I have used something like a proto-V5 loresheet that fundamentally alters the Tremere, because if your ass belongs to the Pyramid, then <i><b>your ass belongs to the Pyramid</b></i>. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I apply this logic to classes i don't like, It'd be black mark against me to deny people say.....d&amp;d tieflings I'm also hard line on pyramid. You want to play Tremere you play Tremere not some hippy anarch with 3 dots in green path as core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-28-2021, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T18:11:01-08:00","id":1469136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469127#post1469127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that keeping Thaumaturgy Out of Clan for everyone solves everything I could reasonably have against it or the Tremere. As a clan of hermetic vampires I think their concept work, magic or not. As an extraneous thing that any character can learn if and when the ST presents an opportunity to them, Thaumaturgy works.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s take is valid. Taking Thaumaturgy out of the game don't really hurt it that much and no one's required to like the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting suggestion around revised was the tremere clan flaw is thaumaturgy is out of clan for xp. For my own games I've always insisted path of blood as primary for all pcs and had a rough of list of off limits paths. I also had a hidden rule that it was impossible to develope healing/prophecy rituals and paths due to limitations of vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T19:10:21-08:00","id":1469138,"title":"","content":"I often use Thaumaturgy, Koldunic Sorcery, Necromancy and the rest of Blood Magic along with the Sorcery book as the base for Mages. I don't think Vampire and Mage, or any other game line other than Mummy work well together, but Blood Magic is worth keeping for mages. It works wonderfully as a &quot;true Mage&quot; magic system that just needs a little tweaking here and there.<br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar408_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"408\" data-vbnamecard=\"408\">nothing</a> that nothing is lost when vampires can't do magic, and from experience the game is better for it. Blood Magic was never well thought out or balanced, and only grew worse over time. I have had players with Thaumaturgy in games though, sometimes player fun trumps my personal preference for a chronicle.<br /> <br /> That said I'm not really feeling the list of 5 disciplines, but I wonder if 5th had actually tried something like that, all shifting powers in one, all control powers in one, etc... down to just a small handful of disciplines if they might have made an interesting edition when someone with Shifting had an ability from 5 different classic disciplines by the time they got the 5th dot, it would be a lot harder to gage your opponent, and prepare for a fight and you could probably come up with some pretty interesting combinations. looking at say Auspex, it feels a little weird that everyone with it eventually can read objects history and astral travel like Dr. Strange, just a couple of things I don't find very vampire like, but no doubt got added when they were trying to come up with 5 powers for each discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T19:48:06-08:00","id":1469141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469135#post1469135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...yes but I said fuelled by blood not fuelled by the path of blood. all thaumaturgical path require blood to work so are implicitly blood magics right?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking right past each other, like I was afraid, but this - this is my original bone of contention (and the only point I'll be addressing). <i><b>HOW</b></i> do Thaumaturgical Paths require blood to work? Show me an example, because it's not mechanical - it's a Willpower roll. There's no Blood Point expenditure, and aside from Path of Blood, <i>no other Path has anything at all to do with blood</i>. Even rituals are (usually) Occult rolls without having to sacrifice a goat <i>or shed any blood whatsoeve</i><i>r</i>. So unless you and I have different definitions of the word 'fueled' how does Blood Sorcery have anything at all to do with blood? It's just dime-store hedge magic with fangs. And if the counter argument is &quot;The magic comes from the blood,&quot; then <u><b>all</b></u> Disciplines are Blood Magic; the distinction is irrelevant; and Thaumaturgy sucks even more because it was <i>purposefully made</i> to be dime-store hedge magic with fangs.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T20:06:08-08:00","id":1469142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469141#post1469141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking right past each other, like I was afraid, but this - this is my original bone of contention (and the only point I'll be addressing). <i><b>HOW</b></i> do Thaumaturgical Paths require blood to work? Show me an example, because it's not mechanical - it's a Willpower roll. There's no Blood Point expenditure,</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't checked second edition yet, but in both V20 and Revised VtM, and even in the original Vampire: the Dark Ages really, using a thaumaturgy path requires spending a blood point.<br /> <br /> V20, p213:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each time the character invokes one of the powers<br /> of a Thaumaturgical path, the thaumaturge\u2019s player<br /> must spend a blood point and make a Willpower roll<br /> against a difficulty equal to the power\u2019s level +3. </div> </div> </div>VtDA, p164:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each time these individual powers are employed, a Blood Point<br /> must be spent and a Willpower roll must be made against a difficulty<br /> of the power\u2019s level + 3. </div> </div> </div>Same deal in revised, page 178, and at this point I'd pretty much just be copy and pasting essentially identical text from each book.<br /> <br /> So, it is mechanical unless I'm missing something there.<br /> <br /> There are certainly other supplements that go deep into the idea of how blood fuels thaumaturgy on a more mystical or philosophical or whatever level, but just to solely address the idea of the mechanical for the moment, Thaumaturgical Paths working off blood has been true since at least 1996.<br /> <br /> Are you referring to some 1e thing? Or maybe second edition?<br /> <br /> edit: Even in 5th ed, Blood Sorcery looks to generally require rouse checks to use, that edition's replacement for blood points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-28-2021, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T20:13:40-08:00","id":1469143,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a> I stand corrected. Thank you for pointing that out.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T20:38:03-08:00","id":1469144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469102#post1469102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Blood Brothers, Gargoyles, Lamia, Samedi, Maeghar and Baali are all <i>fucking awesome</i>. (if you ignore a few shitty texts)<br /> Most are decent. I quite like the variants of the big clans that don't stand apart too much. Lineage should be more than just how many people separate you from an antideluvian.<br /> <br /> The Ahrimanes, TrBr, Evil angles or whatever, Kiasyd... there's more than a few iffy things there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood Brothers are just the weirdest take on a bloodline, they make 10 times more sense as enpowered ghouls rather them actual vampires, Gargoyles are a much better line than them. Same for the Samedi and Lamia. Maeghar are a bloodline in the loosest sense of the word, making them a &quot;bloodline&quot; is really limiting to the concept of an embraced changeling, and the Baali might as well be their own thread. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469102#post1469102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Vampire wrapped around their specialist discipline isn't a problem. Several of the Big Clans frequently have members than do that, and it' not a problem. Thaumaturgy, Vicissitude, Obtenebration, Protean, Obfuscate...<br /> Bloodline are a nice curveball for when your players have slain their 9th Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a problem IMO and I'm glad its gone. It makes those Clans severely more one-note, and old Thaumarturgy has its own host of issues. <br /> <br /> Which is the current <i>subject </i>of this thread so I'll share my opinion on it. <br /> <br /> Vampire Sorcery should, first and foremost, be focused on blood. Not just spending blood, but everything. Which is why I enjoy the new takes on it (even if I few it lacks some raw power), especially thematically. Blood magic shouldn't make other disciplines redundant, the Tremere are at their strongest for me when they are masters of unknowable magics of the blood, rather than wizards conjuring candy and poisoned apples from thin air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T23:02:36-08:00","id":1469148,"title":"","content":"It ain't one-note, Lasombra are more diverse than Ventrue, a clan with three of the most common disciplines available. If you can't think of what to do with your Samedi other than make her an ash pile, you're the problem, not the bloodline. (Granted, The DoC are really, really, really fucking specific, but they're the exception to the rule) <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire Sorcery should, first and foremost, be focused on blood. Not just spending blood, but everything. Which is why I enjoy the new takes on it (even if I few it lacks some raw power), especially thematically </div> </div> </div>This is... kid logic.<br /> &quot;Vampires drink blood, so their magic should be BLOOD MAGIC!!&quot; (and they should all wear black and red and be at least two centuries out of date in terms of fashion. Capes, canes and big collars are a must) <br /> 1- This makes all vampire religions a joke since there obviously isn't anything more to the vampire state. <br /> 2-&quot;Blood magic&quot; is vague as fuck. It usually includes shit like curses or anything dark and gritty that doesn't have anything to do with blood. <br /> 3- The Tremere/FoS/Assamite sorcerers are wasting their time, with their limited purview it should take them a decade to learn everything, and then they're good to go never use it again. Actually why would Tremere bother recruiting so many vampires if there's no capability to diversify their portfolio? In V20 a chantry could have a host of different thaumaturgical experts, in V5 they're all going to be the same... why? Five people with the exact same skillset devalues that skill. As you said &quot; the Tremere are at their strongest for me when they are masters of unknowable magics of the blood&quot; but when they've got like, 20 spells, you can hardly describe such magic as unknowable. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy isn't imbalanced. It's simply more flashy. Any Discipline&gt;Any path. Common disciplines are simply more broadly applicable, there's so many different ways to use Potence, Animalism, Dominate, but only so many ways to use Movement of the mind, a homunculi, or the Path of Corruption. The Rare disciplines are more powerful; Obtenernation 5&gt;&gt;&gt;Movement of the Mind 5. It's easy to get jealous of the guy with glowing blue lightning on his arms but you've got to remember you're ripping steel apart with your bare hands, jumping 20 metres and climbing things that can't be climbed with normal human limits. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T01:16:59-08:00","id":1469156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469141#post1469141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking right past each other, like I was afraid, but this - this is my original bone of contention (and the only point I'll be addressing). <i><b>HOW</b></i> do Thaumaturgical Paths require blood to work? Show me an example, because it's not mechanical - it's a Willpower roll. There's no Blood Point expenditure, and aside from Path of Blood, <i>no other Path has anything at all to do with blood</i>. Even rituals are (usually) Occult rolls without having to sacrifice a goat <i>or shed any blood whatsoeve</i><i>r</i>. So unless you and I have different definitions of the word 'fueled' how does Blood Sorcery have anything at all to do with blood? It's just dime-store hedge magic with fangs. And if the counter argument is &quot;The magic comes from the blood,&quot; then <u><b>all</b></u> Disciplines are Blood Magic; the distinction is irrelevant; and Thaumaturgy sucks even more because it was <i>purposefully made</i> to be dime-store hedge magic with fangs.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there's a blood point expenditure I havnt got access to 20th but it's right there on page 178 section Paths paragraph 3 In revised.<br /> <br /> Edit-okay in v20 page 213 says the same, top paragraph. Blood expenditure. We're not talking over each other, you're incorrect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-29-2021, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T01:45:06-08:00","id":1469157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469144#post1469144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire Sorcery should, first and foremost, be focused on blood. Not just spending blood, but everything. Which is why I enjoy the new takes on it (even if I few it lacks some raw power), especially thematically. Blood magic shouldn't make other disciplines redundant, the Tremere are at their strongest for me when they are masters of unknowable magics of the blood, rather than wizards conjuring candy and poisoned apples from thin air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not going to lie, i find blood magics bring entirely centered on blood or blood based effects is visually and thematically silly. It's roughly the equivalent of suggesting werewolf theurges shoot glowing wolves out their hands or some other wolf based visual whenever they do quasi magical effects.<br /> <br /> Edit:although I'll conceed having blood as a suffix for loads of destructive powers is metal AF. Bloodstorm, bloodrecutted, bloodied condemnation etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-29-2021, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T02:29:46-08:00","id":1469158,"title":"","content":"Even Cruac, which is about as blood happy as you can make something, has plenty of powers that don't involve blood beyond activation. Because the mystic logic behind Cruac is that it uses blood as a conduit for the power of the Beast, and that's what you're really unleashing with its rituals (which is also part of the reason Cruac is especially damaging to Humanity compared to other VtR Disciplines). When a Cruac user uses their magic to let them deal lots of damage with just a touch of their hands, they don't need to start sweating blood, or cut their palm open, or something first. Their blood isn't what does the damage. Their blood is what drew out the wrath and rage of their Beast, and the ritual bound that condenses anger into their hands so powerfully it hurts other people with just contact.<br /> <br /> For me at least, the &quot;blood magic needs to be bloody,&quot; is just putting aesthetics over coherence.<br /> <br /> If Thaumaturgy works by letting vampires use the magical power in vitae to empower debased forms of mortal hedge magics, then there's no need for extra &quot;bloodiness&quot; even if Thaumaturgy could use some more flavor on the &quot;debased&quot; side of things that can help visualize how vitae empowered magic is tainted by the curse in the blood. <br /> <br /> Otherwise we're getting very quickly into less &quot;blood sorcery should be about blood&quot; and more into just having a blood manipulation Discipline that doesn't have anything to do with ritualized mystic powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T04:49:58-08:00","id":1469164,"title":"","content":"What I personally see at the core of some complains about Disciplines, magic and bloodlines is a determination to have the game as strict as possible.<br /> <br /> RPG needs variety. Players and Storytellers alike need tools to explore many concepts and ideas, executions serious and silly, to their hearts content. They have a right and need to explore the themes of the game in unexpected ways.<br /> <br /> Every RPG works like that. A setting needs coherence, but also need options.<br /> <br /> Vampire is, you know, about vampires. <i><b>Every single PC</b></i> is a vampire or at least vampire-related. The whole game is already single-note in this without a need to make its vampires being single-note themselves.<br /> <br /> In a crossover game or any game where vampires aren't the single focus it's perfectly ok to have your vampires being all &quot;normal&quot; to the last one. Because you have other things to add variety. But a game about vampires does needs vampires that cover as broad a spectrum of possibilities as possible.<br /> <br /> Cr\u00faac works because it's not the only magic in VtR.<br /> <br /> And a lot of people are still adamant about &quot;the true folklore of vampires&quot;. BS on flames! True folklore of vampires is at best a dead dude fucking his wife in her sleep, or a blackened corpse stumbling around in robes. Vampires are a pop-culture thing, period. Even Dhampirs actually have more legit folklore about them (the children of the dead dude after he fucked his wife).<br /> <br /> So, please, less purism here. Sparkling vampires <b>are not</b> a blasphemy, nor is Vampire Harry Potter. Weird bloodlines are as ok as it gets. Signature powers are a staple of fiction and do not mean their users are &quot;just their powers&quot;. And it wasn't removed from V5, all the signature powers are still there or being re-added, because they're <b><i>signatures</i></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T09:38:17-08:00","id":1469179,"title":"","content":"I agree with Karos.<br /> <br /> Though I would not mind to see more alternatives to choose from in each discipline.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468860#post1468860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>1) Animalism - </b>Control animals and the nature of animals.<br /> <b>2) Auspex - </b>Augmenting senses including attuning them to 'magic', or giving you extra-sensory perception.<br /> <b>3) Blood Sorcery -</b> Vampiric magic (typically in the form of exerting 'control' over the blood), combining the schools of practice.<br /> <b>4) Celerity - </b>Speed and grace.<br /> <b>5) Dominate -</b> Direct mental control over others, including memories.<br /> <b>6) Fortitude -</b> Greater resistance to damage physical or mental.<br /> <b>7) Obfuscate -</b> Misdirecting senses to go unnoticed.<br /> <b>8) Oblivion - </b>Control/utilisation of the Abyss/Shadowlands and their manifestations in the skinlands.<br /> <b>9) Potence -</b> Greater strength channelled to various effects.<br /> <b>10) Presence -</b> Control over the emotions of others.<br /> <b>11) Protean - </b>Shape-changing and manipulating organic matter.<br /> <b>12) Thin-Blood Alchemy -</b> Altering the properties of Thin-Blood vitae with certain ingredients. <i>(The only one that I'm shakey on really, still feels like they just wanted to give something cool to the Thin-Bloods. It could just as easily have been another type of Blood Sorcery, predominantly used by Thin-Bloods and requiring their vitae.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I loved vampire and I have played it sice 1991 (at least I loved 1st to 3rd edition, everything that came between 3rd and 5th are abominations). V20 to me ruined a lot of fun and felt like it were more suited to numbercrunching munchkins for those who wanted to play 4th generation alien-infested Tzimisce on various paths - at least that is what I experienced). I also hate how they ruined some disciplines in v20. <br /> <br /> V5 for me and the three groups i play in and ST i what we wanted from vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T11:26:12-08:00","id":1469184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469164#post1469164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a lot of people are still adamant about &quot;the true folklore of vampires&quot;. BS on flames! True folklore of vampires is at best a dead dude fucking his wife in her sleep, or a blackened corpse stumbling around in robes. Vampires are a pop-culture thing, period. Even Dhampirs actually have more legit folklore about them (the children of the dead dude after he fucked his wife).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As a side the only folklore I could find on direct manipulation of blood was a monster who makes babies out of period blood.....neither were vampires.<br /> <br /> So theirs that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-29-2021, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T11:59:21-08:00","id":1469186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469179#post1469179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 to me ruined a lot of fun and felt like it were more suited to numbercrunching munchkins for those who wanted to play 4th generation alien-infested Tzimisce on various paths - at least that is what I experienced). I also hate how they ruined some disciplines in v20.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the first person I see with such an opinion on V20. I mean, I've seen some with indifference, but this?<br /> <br /> I'm really curious, why do you think so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T04:30:32-08:00","id":1469246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469186#post1469186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're the first person I see with such an opinion on V20. I mean, I've seen some with indifference, but this?<br /> <br /> I'm really curious, why do you think so?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I started playing RPGs with my parents when i was 7 or 8 years old, i think. Don't longer rememember how young i was but it ws ages ago. They had wonderful campaign of Traveller that I had been sitting in on for quite some time to listen as they and their friends had so much fun and on saturdays the stories they made were like my good night stories. Exciting space adventures and battles against pirates exploration of wonderful alien worlds. It was better than any cinema.<br /> <br /> So when i was old enough me and my best friend (her parents were in the gaming group as well) were asked if we wanted to join, and both of us agreed and that campaign lasted until we went to university. What I loved about it was that there was this huge story that unfolded, even though we were not part of all of it. The universe was moving and alive. <br /> <br /> Vampire, since its beginnings, had such wonderfull lore that was tied to the metaplot, just like Traveller. the way that revised edition built up a huge meta plot that culminated into the Gehenna book was something special. Again it felt like each book was part of this metaplot. Each book published moved the plot further and further along its path. <br /> <br /> When V20 ws published it first felt like white wolf was thinking that &quot;<i>People loved all of the books up to the Gehenna stories, Requim is not loved s much by old players, well, time to cash in on those who did not jump ship and lets just do a new edition to make money and disguise it as 20 year celebration&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> But without the metaplot that is tied to the universe, V20 felt like GURPS or Dungeons and Dragons, but with vampires instead of other races. I do not complain about the books the books from v20 I have seen has been from OPP and as always they have a quality above most companies in the RPG world. What I dont like was that the game was no longer tied to the moving universe and thus lacked a lot.<br /> <br /> The books added a power level that I do not enjoy and with that changed a few disciplines so that it was no longer fun to play a high generation vampire as you needed your bloodpool high in order to use said disciplines.<br /> <br /> I have played a few V20 campaign, but even with truely great STs the game felt lacking and I did not like the change they made to some disciplines.<br /> <br /> That is the main concerns i have, but there are more. But I am too tired to sit infront of a screen as I have been working a 14 hour shift at the hospital all night and the bus is nearly at my stop now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T07:52:38-08:00","id":1469252,"title":"","content":"I love the v20 books because they're so comprehensive. Sounds like the problem is you enjoy the story they make for more than just inspiration/ideas and that's cool too.<br /> <br /> For me the meta plot was pretty terrible after first edition set the world, later books really lost the plot. I mean sure, Baba Yaga runs Russia, that's cool, but Chicago by Night is Chicago by night vol 1 in my world and the game decides who lives and dies, there is no under a blood red moon or second edition telling me who got purged. The Sabbat never took out the east coast destroying half the country for games during Revised. Signature characters are silly PC's of the writers I ignore, as the books tend to ignore game mechanics. Revised had such a terrible feel/vibe for me, it made the world feel cartoony, as did clans like the Tzimisce and Lasombra to be honest, so there is my unpopular preference. The first adventure in the back of the core rule book felt like the perfect tone, then they completely screwed the mood they set with the silly screen adventure that changed all the characters they had just written at a core level. For me DAV20 is my main go to for rules, the world is mainly what came first, what I set up, plus what happens in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T00:44:05-08:00","id":1469702,"title":"","content":"IMO the amount of disciplines is alright, but 3 main disciplines for every major clan seems too few. Hecata is pretty revolutionary, because blood lines can swap certain disciplines with other ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T02:26:35-08:00","id":1469709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469702#post1469702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO the amount of disciplines is alright</div> </div> </div> </div> in which edition? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but 3 main disciplines for every major clan seems too few. Hecata is pretty revolutionary, because blood lines can swap certain disciplines with other ones. </div> </div> </div>Most the clans in the game had a bloodline with alternate disciplines.<br /> <br /> Three disciplines gives each clan a strong identity. Four weakens a lot of clans too much, while also discouraging Out of Clan choices that can make a character more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T02:49:19-08:00","id":1469711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469702#post1469702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO the amount of disciplines is alright, but 3 main disciplines for every major clan seems too few. Hecata is pretty revolutionary, because blood lines can swap certain disciplines with other ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking V5, right? Because we've been discussing all editions and this makes a lot of difference.<br /> <br /> And Hecata isn't revolutionary. The revolution was the opposite, they reduced access to bloodlines with alternate spreads on each clan. All the Hecata members already existed as having their individual spreads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T03:43:51-08:00","id":1469715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469711#post1469711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're talking V5, right? Because we've been discussing all editions and this makes a lot of difference.<br /> <br /> And Hecata isn't revolutionary. The revolution was the opposite, they reduced access to bloodlines with alternate spreads on each clan. All the Hecata members already existed as having their individual spreads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, sorry. I mean V5. I think that having optional main disciplines is a pretty cool system and I didn't even think about it before reading Cults (except for Antitribu).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T04:04:46-08:00","id":1469716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469715#post1469715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that having optional main disciplines is a pretty cool system and I didn't even think about it before reading Cults (except for Antitribu).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, it just isn't new. A lot of clans throughout the years got to have distinct lineages or castes that offered a different set of Disciplines in exactly the same way the Hecata does, except they didn't demanded expending points on it before.<br /> <br /> And that includes the Hecata itself, because every lineage of it was previously its own thing with their own discipline spreads. Making them work as a single clan and then &quot;selling&quot; their individuality back as lore sheets isn't exactly what I would call revolutionary.<br /> <br /> But a Merit to let any vampire to trade a single In-Clan for another, <b>that</b> would be pretty rad. We could have a list of four to six Disciplines for each clan, three main and one to three that a character can trade with Advantage points.<br /> <br /> On the number of Disciplines, I think the number is right, the spread isn't. Mashing up Necromancy and Obtenebration into Oblivion was a poor choice, and Thin Blood Alchemy is an interesting idea but doesn't quite work and could be traded for a broader rule on how Thin Bloods learn Disciplines, then included in Thaumaturgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T04:39:19-08:00","id":1469718,"title":"","content":"TBA doesn't make sense within the context of the WoD and as a gameplay element it causes more problems than it solves, so it really shouldn't exist<br /> <br /> trying to keep an open mind: Obtenebration wouldn't be a terrible path for necromancy. But the way oblivion's done is so bad that it's best ignored entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T05:50:51-08:00","id":1469721,"title":"","content":"What does TBA mean in this context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T06:00:21-08:00","id":1469722,"title":"","content":"Thin Blood alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T09:31:23-08:00","id":1469743,"title":"","content":"3 in-clans work really well, and getting an out of clan isn't that big of a deal unless you want to level it really high. Its why the couple merits in V5 that allow you to get an extra in-clan are only a good investment once you level a discipline to 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T15:52:33-08:00","id":1469775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469718#post1469718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBA doesn't make sense within the context of the WoD and as a gameplay element it causes more problems than it solves, so it really shouldn't exist<br /> <br /> trying to keep an open mind: Obtenebration wouldn't be a terrible path for necromancy. But the way oblivion's done is so bad that it's best ignored entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thin Blood alchemy isn't very good and doesn't really mesh well with the thematic traits of thin bloods<br /> Personally I'd just put some of the unique powers into blood sorcery and put a cap on disciplines at 1 with some perks. You want to play a crappy vampire then play a crappy vampire, because that's something I can see as interesting.<br /> <br /> Then again I havnt seen anyone want to play a thin blood since 2007 so I'm curious how popular a choice they really are","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T16:47:20-08:00","id":1469783,"title":"","content":"If thin-bloods had to invest in disciplines, but were capped at 1, I expect that a lot of player characters would collect which ever ones have useful 1 dot powers that don't scale with the discipline, so they'd end up being the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T02:53:16-08:00","id":1469815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469783#post1469783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If thin-bloods had to invest in disciplines, but were capped at 1, I expect that a lot of player characters would collect which ever ones have useful 1 dot powers that don't scale with the discipline, so they'd end up being the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>In most cases, the first dot of any discipline is something broadly applicable; easy to use, minimal consequences, with a lot of utility. while later powers have a narrower scope or consequences for using them (Which could be simple like costing more blood or willpower or something less concrete like being flagrant masquerade violations) There are of course some glaring exceptions to this (obfuscate 1, Chimistry, Temporis thinking it's a Sphere) but that's something most people think is a flaw. <br /> <br /> Also like, Thin bloods had the ability to obtain 4/3 dots of disciplines (depending on whether they were 14th/15th generation) before the last edition changed the sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T05:06:33-08:00","id":1469820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469815#post1469815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most cases, the first dot of any discipline is something broadly applicable; easy to use, minimal consequences, with a lot of utility. while later powers have a narrower scope or consequences for using them (Which could be simple like costing more blood or willpower or something less concrete like being flagrant masquerade violations) There are of course some glaring exceptions to this (obfuscate 1, Chimistry, Temporis thinking it's a Sphere) but that's something most people think is a flaw.<br /> <br /> Also like, Thin bloods had the ability to obtain 4/3 dots of disciplines (depending on whether they were 14th/15th generation) before the last edition changed the sheets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I referred back to the V5 core and only two or three disciplines have that problem when limited to one dot. While one more die in charisma rolls or the health track is rather meagre, it is likely to come into a lot of situations. And I was assuming that each new 1st dot of a discipline would cost 7xp (it might even be 6xp if they count as Caitiff), rather than the 10 of V&lt;5, so lateral discipline development could cost more xp than it's worth, even without the option of linear development<i>.</i><br /> <br /> Based on V&lt;5 RAW, thin-bloods still have a lot of room to specialise in chosen disciplines, so there's less incentive to be a jack of all trades than if they were limited to 1 dot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T06:37:28-08:00","id":1469829,"title":"","content":"Being limited to 1 or 2 dots but have a lessened cost to buy more powers on the same Discipline (instead of an inability to do so like current RAW) would be interesting. Another option would be to have Merits or whatnot that let them change parameters for a Discipline at a cost, <i>a la</i> Metamagic Feats. Both solutions would play on TB being weaker, but stranger.<br /> <br /> I don't think a cap on Disciplines is needed, though, as long as their use of them have other attached effects to fulfill this theme. The use of Disciplines could have a greater cost or Side Effects the Thin Blood can't suppress. As long as it makes the decision to use them harder and the effects stranger for other vampires and less showy for witnesses, I'm good with it, even if the result isn't really less powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T08:46:18-08:00","id":1469841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1468848#post1468848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not allowed to make this a V5 bashing thread but V5's disciplines are not <i>well defined</i> they're loose collections of powers held together by theme. V1 Fortitude negates more and more damage, That's well defined. V5 fortitude is anything from &quot;you have more health&quot; to &quot;you ignore one attack per turn&quot; to &quot;insults upset you less&quot; which is... less cohesive. I'll grant that V5 does a relatively decent job with Presence, but Presence has always been the messy kid in vampire.<br /> <br /> ...and I really hate picking powers, at least how V5 does it.. V5 offers more choices, but as you can only have 5 powers in a discipline, every choice locks you off from another choice. That's very stressful. A linear 1-5 system with some powers having options to buy alternative powers you didn't get is elegant in it's simplicity; There's no overchoice, there's no locking yourself out of a power. When I buy a power in V20, I'm only sacrificing XP and delaying the acquisition of other options. When I buy a power in V5, I need to think deeply about the &quot;build&quot; that I want because there's a hard cap on what I can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. On the other hand, it does result in vampires with a theme. It allows you to make a Ventrue who feels like an icy statue of gods/kings, and a Gangrel who feels like an utter savage revealing in pain, even his own.<br /> <br /> Going into other disciplines, it allows you to create a Malkavian who is haunted by visions of the future, and a Tremere who casually sees through the inferior parlor tricks of those trying to hide or sneak up on him via his mastery of enlightened awareness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T10:39:04-08:00","id":1469855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1469841#post1469841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true. On the other hand, it does result in vampires with a theme. It allows you to make a Ventrue who feels like an icy statue of gods/kings, and a Gangrel who feels like an utter savage revealing in pain, even his own.<br /> <br /> Going into other disciplines, it allows you to create a Malkavian who is haunted by visions of the future, and a Tremere who casually sees through the inferior parlor tricks of those trying to hide or sneak up on him via his mastery of enlightened awareness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V5 doesn't really tie the options with Clans, but with Disciplines, \u00bfdoesn't it?. In general I think more choice it's better than less choice, but I'm not sure how I feel about non-Malkavian Auspex users having the same access to the *same* oracular power that Malkavians would have. Especialy if we want it to represent a general &quot;theme&quot;: <b>Haunted</b> <b>by visions of the future </b>for the Malkavian, sure, but if I'm not mistaken any vampire with Auspex can buy that ... It could result in the opposite of what you describe: vampires w/o such general themes (each vampire being a singular, unique, creature)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T03:28:54-08:00","id":1470021,"title":"","content":"Looking at the discipline lineup of the 14 clans, I'm seeing more discipline overlap than in previous editions, although not as dramatic as anticipated. <br /> How are people approaching the fact a lot of clans could in theory use formerly unique powers? I'm probably going to put a hard no on having them unless tutored by the clan in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T04:17:32-08:00","id":1470025,"title":"","content":"If there is a really good reason, I'd allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T08:48:01-08:00","id":1470036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468828-how-many-disciplines-should-there-be?p=1470021#post1470021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the discipline lineup of the 14 clans, I'm seeing more discipline overlap than in previous editions, although not as dramatic as anticipated.<br /> How are people approaching the fact a lot of clans could in theory use formerly unique powers? I'm probably going to put a hard no on having them unless tutored by the clan in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I allow it. I don't think anything is gained by making a homebrew ruling like that, besides limiting players options and hamfistedly going back to previous editions. Players usually take powers that fit their characters anyway in my experience, and there isn't any power that I find considerably stronger than the rest to consider power gaming, especially when you take into account that there are a limited number of powers you can pick. <br /> <br /> Amalgams that are in-Clan for other Clans besides the &quot;intended&quot; ones are Chimerstry for the Ministry, which I think is a perfect fit, as cult leaders conjuring illusions to mislead a crowd is just on point, and the Salubri ones, which I don't think anyone would willingly pick unless it made <i><b>a lot </b></i>of sense for their character. <br /> <br /> As for the rest, they are already paying out of clan costs, and as I said before, the powers aren't so much stronger that they warrant additional limitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}